.TH BRIC 1 "July 2026" "BRIC Archive 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bric \- create, inspect, search, monitor and restore encrypted BRIC tape archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bric backup
.I PROJECT SOURCE
.RI [ --as " LOGICAL_ROOT" ]
.RI [ --force ]
.RI [ --wait ]
.br
.B bric restore
.I PROJECT DEST
.RI [ --file " REL" ]
.RI [ --run " RUN_ID" ]
.RI [ --wait ]
.br
.B bric status
.RI [ --project " PROJECT" ]
.br
.B bric list
.RI [ --long ]
.RI [ --all ]
.br
.B bric contents
.I PROJECT
.RI [ --run " RUN_ID" ]
.RI [ --history ]
.RI [ --type " TYPE" ]
.RI [ --long ]
.RI [ --limit " N" ]
.RI [ --offset " N" ]
.br
.B bric find
.I PROJECT QUERY
.RI [ --run " RUN_ID" ]
.RI [ --history ]
.RI [ --type " TYPE" ]
.RI [ --long ]
.RI [ --limit " N" ]
.RI [ --offset " N" ]
.br
.B bric exclusions
PROJECT [--run RUN_ID]
.br
.B bric jobs
.br
.B bric log
.RI [ JOB_ID | PID ]
.br
.B bric cancel
.IR JOB_ID | PID
.br
.B bric version
.br
.B bric help
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bric
is the user-facing command for the BRIC encrypted tape archive system.
It loads the site configuration and personal archive environment automatically,
performs operational preflight checks for backup and restore, and dispatches the
requested operation.
.PP
In local mode, backup and restore run as detached background jobs by default.
The command returns a job identifier, PID and log path.  Use
.BR "bric jobs" ,
.BR "bric log" ,
and
.B "bric cancel"
to manage these jobs.  The
.B --wait
option keeps backup or restore in the foreground.
.PP
The short positional forms shown in SYNOPSIS are intended for normal use.
Equivalent long forms are also accepted:
.PP
.nf
bric backup  --project NAME --source DIR [--as LOGICAL_ROOT] [--exclude RELPATH ...] [--source-change-policy strict|record] [--force] [--wait]
bric restore --project NAME --dest DIR [--file REL] [--run RUN_ID] [--require-destination-verify] [--wait]
.fi
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "backup " "PROJECT SOURCE" " [--as LOGICAL_ROOT] [--exclude RELPATH ...] [--source-change-policy strict|record] [--force] [--wait]"
Create an encrypted archive backup of
.IR SOURCE
under the logical project name
.IR PROJECT .
In local mode the operation is detached unless
.B --wait
is supplied.  The source is read by GNU tar and catalogued while it is archived;
there is no separate full per-file planning scan.  Before reservation BRIC validates source readability. By default every unreadable or untraversable
included path is reported as a warning and the preflight then fails, so no tape is reserved. With
.B --force
BRIC skips only precisely identified unreadable paths, logs every omission and records each one in
the encrypted project catalog with reason force-unreadable. The independent
.B --exclude RELPATH
option is an intentional operator-selected scope exclusion applied before readability checking and
recorded with reason user-declared; it is not a permission failure and does not require --force.
Unknown traversal/I/O failures remain fatal. Source changes detected by GNU tar are fatal by default; explicit
.B --source-change-policy record
accepts only FILE_CHANGED_DURING_READ diagnostics and stores them in the encrypted project catalog.
.PP
.B --as LOGICAL_ROOT
sets the stable single-component logical root used by catalog browsing and single-file restore. If omitted, BRIC uses the basename of the declared source path. The root is catalog metadata only: TAR member names and the on-tape format are unchanged. The root must be one NFC path component of at most 255 bytes; slash, comma, control characters, `.' and `..' are rejected. Reusing a root for a different or unknown canonical source in the same project is rejected before tape reservation.
.TP
.BR "restore " "PROJECT DEST" " [--file REL] [--run RUN_ID] [--require-destination-verify] [--wait]"
Restore a project into
.IR DEST .
Without
.B --run
and without
.B --file
BRIC selects the latest CLOSED run, preserving the historical full-restore behavior. With
.B --file
use LOGICAL_ROOT/RELATIVE_PATH to select the newest CLOSED run containing that logical key; BRIC restores the physical run-relative member below DEST/LOGICAL_ROOT. With an explicit
.B --run
BRIC accepts both the logical form and the historical bare run-relative path. An ambiguous bare automatic lookup is rejected. In local mode the operation is
detached unless
.B --wait
is supplied.
.TP
.BR "status" " [--project PROJECT]"
Show recent archive runs, their lifecycle state, chunk counts, completed chunks
and total size.  Active local runs also display live file, byte and chunk
progress.  Without
.B --project
only runs owned by the current user are shown.
.TP
.BR "list" " [--long] [--all]"
List archived projects.  The
.B --long
form includes run count and assigned tape barcodes.  The
.B --all
option includes projects owned by other users when catalog permissions allow it.
.TP
.BR "contents " "PROJECT" " [--run RUN_ID] [--history] [--type TYPE] [--long] [--limit N] [--offset N]"
List the logical namespace formed from all CLOSED backups of
.IR PROJECT .
Entries are keyed as LOGICAL_ROOT/RELATIVE_PATH; for duplicate keys the newest CLOSED run containing the path wins. Files found only in older runs remain visible because there are no tombstones, so the union is not a filesystem snapshot. No tape is mounted or read; the information comes from the cluster catalog.
Use
.B --history
to show every version with its run id, or
.B --run
to select one exact CLOSED run,
.B --type
to restrict results to
.BR all ,
.BR file ,
.BR dir
or
.BR link ,
and
.B --long
to include type, byte size and UTC modification time.  The default limit is
1000 entries.  A normal user may inspect only projects owned by that user.
.TP
.BR "find " "PROJECT QUERY" " [--run RUN_ID] [--history] [--type TYPE] [--long] [--limit N] [--offset N]"
Search case-insensitively for
.I QUERY
anywhere in the complete logical path. By default all CLOSED runs participate and the newest version wins per logical key; --history shows all versions and --run selects one exact CLOSED run. No tape is read. The default limit is 200 matches.  Spaces and shell
metacharacters in the query should be quoted.
.TP
.BR "exclusions " "PROJECT" " [--run RUN_ID]"
Show explicit source subtrees intentionally omitted from the selected CLOSED run. No tape is read.
.TP
.BR "source-changes " "PROJECT" " [--run RUN_ID]"
Show source-consistency semantics and recorded FILE_CHANGED_DURING_READ diagnostics for a CLOSED run.
No tape is read. Paths are displayed using GNU tar escape quoting when required.

.TP
.B jobs
List local background jobs.  Output includes job identifier, PID, state,
action, project and start/end timestamps.
.TP
.BR "log" " [JOB_ID|PID]"
Follow the last 80 lines of a local background job log.  With no argument, use
the newest recorded job.  The command follows new output until interrupted,
typically with Ctrl-C.
.TP
.BR "cancel" " JOB_ID|PID"
Request termination of a running local background job and its process group.
The archive run is then recorded as cancelled or failed according to the point
at which termination occurred.
.TP
.B version
Show the authoritative installed release marker from /opt/bric2/RELEASE.
.TP
.BR "help" " [COMMAND]"
Show general help or command-specific help.  The forms
.B "bric COMMAND --help"
and
.B "bric --help COMMAND"
and
.B "bric COMMAND help"
are equivalent. Help and malformed-command validation occur before operational preflight or background job creation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --force
For backup only, continue after preflight finds precisely identified unreadable paths. Such paths
are excluded from that run, logged completely, and cataloged as force-unreadable omissions. This is
not equivalent to --skip-preflight and does not suppress unclassified traversal or I/O errors.
.TP
.B --wait
Run backup or restore in the foreground and return only when the operation
finishes or fails.
.TP
.BI "--project " PROJECT
Select a project by logical name.
.TP
.BI "--source " DIR
Specify the source directory for a backup.
.TP
.BI "--dest " DIR
Specify the restore destination directory.
.TP
.BI "--file " REL
Restore only one path relative to the archived project root.
.TP
.BI "--run " RUN_ID
Select a specific archive run instead of automatic latest-CLOSED selection.
For
.B restore ,
.B contents
and
.B find
the selected run must belong to the named project; catalog browsing accepts only
.B CLOSED
runs.
.TP
.BI "--query " TEXT
Specify the search text for the long form of
.BR "bric find" .
.TP
.B --long
Show extended columns with
.BR "bric list" ,
.B "bric contents"
or
.BR "bric find" .
.TP
.BI "--type " TYPE
Filter catalog browsing to
.BR all ,
.BR file ,
.BR dir
or
.BR link .
.TP
.BI "--limit " N
Limit the number of catalog paths printed.  A value of zero disables the limit.
Defaults are 1000 for
.B contents
and 200 for
.BR find .
.TP
.BI "--offset " N
Skip the first
.I N
matching catalog entries, for pagination.
.TP
.B --all
Include all visible projects with
.BR "bric list" .
.TP
.B --skip-preflight
Advanced diagnostic option accepted before
.B backup
or
.BR restore .
It bypasses operational safety checks and is discouraged for normal use.
.SH RUN STATES
.TP
.B PLANNING
The run has been created and initial tape capacity is being reserved.  In the
tar-driven local pipeline this is not a full source-tree scan.
.TP
.B RESERVED
Initial PRIMARY and BACKUP tape capacity has been reserved.  The run may be
waiting for the producer slot.
.TP
.B PRODUCING
BRIC is reading the source with tar, creating encrypted chunks and publishing
them to the QNAP bus.
.TP
.B DRAINING
Source reading has finished.  BRIC is waiting for every chunk to be written and
verified on both PRIMARY and BACKUP media.
.TP
.B CLOSING
BRIC is writing and verifying the encrypted catalog, escrow and recovery
artifacts used to close the media set.
.TP
.B CLOSED
The backup completed successfully and both tape copies and closing artifacts
were confirmed.
.TP
.B DENIED
The initial reservation was refused before production began.
.TP
.B FAILED
The run stopped because of an operational, filesystem, cryptographic, bus,
tape or verification error.
.TP
.B CANCELLED
The run was explicitly cancelled and reached the cancellation terminal state.
.SH BACKGROUND JOB STATES
.TP
.B RUNNING
The detached supervisor PID is alive.
.TP
.B FINISHED
The detached command exited successfully.
.TP
.B FAILED
The detached command exited unsuccessfully.  Inspect its log and
.B "bric status"
for the archive run result.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.bric/env.sh
Per-user BRIC environment loaded automatically by the command wrapper.
.TP
.I ~/.bric/pids/*.meta
Private metadata for local background jobs, including PID, state and log path.
.TP
.I /var/log/bric/users/USER/jobs/*.log
Centralized stdout/stderr logs for local background backup and restore jobs; ~/.bric/log is the emergency fallback.
.TP
.I ~/.bric/*_user_key.txt
Personal archive key provisioned by the BRIC administrator.  Users must not
remove, replace or share this file.
.TP
.I /etc/bric/bric.conf
Site runtime configuration, when the default location is used.
.TP
.I /opt/bric2/RELEASE
Authoritative installed review and release metadata.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BRIC_RUN_MODE
Selects
.B local
or
.B slurm
execution as configured by the site administrator.
.TP
.B BRIC_USER_ENV_FILE
Overrides the per-user environment file path.  The default is
.IR ~/.bric/env.sh .
.TP
.B BRIC_PID_DIR
Overrides the local background-job metadata directory.
.TP
.B BRIC_BACKGROUND_LOGDIR
Overrides the local background-job log directory.
.TP
.B BRIC_CONFIG
Overrides the site configuration path.  The special value
.B none
disables configuration-file loading and is intended for tests or administration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B bric
returns zero when a synchronous command succeeds or when a detached local job
is successfully started.  A non-zero status indicates invalid arguments,
preflight failure, dispatch failure or failure of a foreground operation.
The final result of a detached operation must be checked with
.BR "bric jobs" ,
.BR "bric status"
or
.BR "bric log" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a backup in the default background mode:
.PP
.nf
bric backup mouse_rnaseq /projects/lab/mouse_rnaseq
.fi
.PP
Inspect active runs and local jobs:
.PP
.nf
bric status
bric jobs
.fi
.PP
Follow a job log by job identifier:
.PP
.nf
bric log backup.mouse_rnaseq.20260728T184852Z.2452031
.fi
.PP
List the project logical namespace without reading tape:
.PP
.nf
bric contents mouse_rnaseq --type file --long
bric contents mouse_rnaseq --history --long
.fi
.PP
Search archived paths case-insensitively:
.PP
.nf
bric find mouse_rnaseq sample01.bam
bric find mouse_rnaseq "raw/2026" --run mouse_rnaseq__20260728T184855Z__0001
.fi
.PP
Restore a complete project in the foreground:
.PP
.nf
bric restore mouse_rnaseq /restore/mouse_rnaseq --wait
.fi
.PP
Restore one file through its logical path, or use the historical bare path with an explicit run:
.PP
.nf
bric restore mouse_rnaseq /restore/one \
    --file mouse_rnaseq/raw/sample01.bam --wait
bric restore mouse_rnaseq /restore/one \
    --file raw/sample01.bam \
    --run mouse_rnaseq__20260728T184855Z__0001 --wait
.fi
.SH NOTES
A successful detached start does not mean the archive has completed.  A backup
is complete only when its run state is
.BR CLOSED .
.PP
Tape hardware preflight is performed on the tape-server host and is not a
substitute for the cluster-side preflight shown by the user command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tar (1),
.BR openssl (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR sbatch (1),
.BR squeue (1)
